      "description": "Define exactProductTree tree as tree.map (fun p => p.1 * p.2), roundedProductTree model tree as tree.map (fun p => model.mul p.1 p.2), and roundedDotProduct model tree as roundedSum model (roundedProductTree model tree), for tree : Tree (\u211d \u00d7 \u211d). Preserve shape and leaf multiplicity."
    },
    {
      "id": "multiplication",
      "description": "Prove IsPerturbation model.u (exactProductTree tree) (roundedProductTree model tree) by structural induction. At each leaf use model.round_spec on the exact product; algebra and abs_mul turn |\u03b4| \u2264 model.u into the required absolute leaf error bound. Use IsPerturbation.node for children. Avoid division by the exact product so zero products are covered."
    },
    {
      "id": "depth-and-smallness",
      "description": "Set d := tree.depth. Use Tree.depth_map to obtain depth d for the rounded product tree. From ((d + 1 : \u2115) : \u211d) * model.u < 1 and model.u_nonneg derive (d : \u211d) * model.u < 1, handling casts explicitly. Obtain 0 \u2264 gamma d model.u using gamma_nonneg."
    },
