    },
    {
      "id": "composition",
      "description": "Use IsPerturbation.trans with first bound model.u and second bound gamma d model.u; discharge second-bound nonnegativity. Rewrite the resulting model.u + gamma d model.u * (1 + model.u) to gamma d model.u + model.u * (1 + gamma d model.u). Apply gamma_step d with original smallness, then IsPerturbation.mono to obtain the requested gamma (d + 1) bound."
    },
    {
      "id": "full-contract",
      "description": "State the universal theorem for every supplied Model and every pair tree under only the specified depth-plus-one smallness: there exists perturbed : Tree \u211d with IsPerturbation (gamma (tree.depth + 1) model.u) (exactProductTree tree) perturbed and perturbed.exactSum = roundedDotProduct model tree. Track each leaf occurrence separately, including repeated values and zero products. A single leaf must still include multiplication rounding; do not replace depth + 1 by depth or relate the final witness only to rounded products."
